<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16470" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēversor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		everto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a subverter</i>, <i>destroyer.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carthaginis et Numantiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 6, 30</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regnorum Priami (Achilles),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 12, 545</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regnorum cometes,</span>”
				i. e. <i>presaging their destruction</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 639</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Part. 30 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hujus imperii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Sest. 7, 17</span></i>
			;  juris humani, <i><span class="en">Plin. 28, 1,
				2, § 6</span></i>: pecuniae (with interceptor), i. e. <i>who squanders it</i>, Cod. Th. 12, 6, 1.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
